---
const { osuYears, michYears, seasonProfiles, provenance } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="lab-shell" data-lab data-season-profiles={JSON.stringify(seasonProfiles)}>
  <header class="lab-header"><div><h1>RIVALRY LAB</h1><span>DERIVED SNAPSHOT · MODEL EN-3.2</span></div></header>
  <nav class="lab-nav" aria-label="Rivalry Lab steps"><button data-screen="matchup" aria-current="step">1 · Matchup</button><button data-screen="tape">2 · Tape</button><button data-screen="pregame">3 · Pregame</button><button data-screen="game">4 · Game</button><button data-screen="postgame">5 · Postgame</button></nav>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="matchup"><h2><span class="osu">OHIO STATE <b data-osu-year>1995</b></span> AGAINST <span class="mich">MICHIGAN <b data-mich-year>2023</b></span>, ON NEUTRAL GROUND.</h2><p class="lede">Pick a season from 1970-2025 for each side. Both are translated into one neutral scoring era, then the game is simulated.</p><div class="selector-box"><label><b class="osu">OHIO STATE</b><select data-osu>{osuYears.map((year: number) => <option value={year} selected={year === 1995}>{year}</option>)}</select><small data-osu-facts>Loading derived season rating...</small></label><label><b class="mich">MICHIGAN</b><select data-mich>{michYears.map((year: number) => <option value={year} selected={year === 2023}>{year}</option>)}</select><small data-mich-facts>Loading derived season rating...</small></label></div><div class="lab-actions"><span>ERA NEUTRAL: each season is translated into a common scoring environment.</span><button class="primary" data-build>BUILD MATCHUP →</button></div></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="tape" hidden><div class="section-title"><h2>TALE OF THE TAPE</h2><span data-context></span></div><div class="tape-table" data-tape></div><section class="season-profiles" aria-label="Selected season profiles" data-profiles></section><section class="provenance" data-testid="snapshot-provenance"><b>SOURCES &amp; PROVENANCE</b><p>Derived ratings: public Rivalry Lab product snapshot, generated {new Date(provenance.generatedAt).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}. The snapshot contains no raw warehouse records.</p><p>Snapshot: {provenance.ratingModelVersion} ratings · {provenance.eraModelVersion} era translation · {provenance.dataSnapshotVersion} data coverage.</p><p>Season identities and every simulation output are labeled observed, derived, or simulated.</p></section><div class="lab-actions"><button class="secondary" data-screen="matchup">← SEASON SELECT</button><button class="primary" data-pregame>SIMULATE MATCHUP →</button></div></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="pregame" hidden><div class="pregame"><section><p>DERIVED PREGAME WIN PROBABILITY · ERA NEUTRAL</p><div class="probability"><div><strong class="osu" data-osu-prob>--%</strong><b>OHIO STATE</b></div><div><strong class="mich" data-mich-prob>--%</strong><b>MICHIGAN</b></div></div><div class="prob-bar"><i data-osu-bar></i><i data-mich-bar></i></div><p>Both teams are scored against the offensive and defensive environment of their own seasons, then translated into a common neutral scoring environment.</p></section><section><p>EXPECTED SCORE</p><strong class="score" data-score>--</strong><small>DERIVED, BEFORE ANY SIMULATION</small></section></div><div class="drivers"><article><b>Ohio State scoring edge</b><em>DERIVED</em><p data-osu-driver></p></article><article><b>Michigan scoring edge</b><em>DERIVED</em><p data-mich-driver></p></article><article><b>Turnover volatility</b><em>SIMULATED</em><p>Seeded drives introduce variance around the derived baseline.</p></article></div><div class="lab-actions controls"><span>RUN SIMULATION</span><button data-run="1">PLAY ONE</button><button data-run="10">BEST OF 10</button><button data-run="100">SIM 100</button><button data-run="1000">SIM 1,000</button><button data-run="10000">SIM 10,000</button><label>SEED <input data-seed value="19952023" /></label></div><details data-chalk><summary>PREGAME CHALK TALK</summary><div data-chalk-panel></div></details></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="game" hidden><div class="game-score" data-game-score></div><section class="timeline" aria-label="Simulated drive timeline" data-timeline></section><div class="game-grid"><article data-turning></article><article data-game-stats></article></div><div class="lab-actions"><button class="secondary" data-rerun>RUN AGAIN WITH NEW SEED</button><button class="primary" data-postgame>VIEW POSTGAME →</button></div></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="postgame" hidden><div class="section-title"><h2>POSTGAME</h2><span data-series-context></span></div><div class="post-tabs" role="tablist"><button role="tab" data-tab="summary">Summary</button><button role="tab" data-tab="stats">Stats</button><button role="tab" data-tab="chalk">Chalk Talk</button></div><section data-post-panel></section><div class="lab-actions"><button class="secondary" data-screen="game">← SINGLE GAME</button><button class="secondary" data-screen="matchup">NEW MATCHUP</button></div></section>
  <footer>ALL SIMULATION OUTPUT IS SYNTHETIC. SEASON RATINGS ARE DERIVED FROM A PUBLIC SNAPSHOT. HEAD-TO-HEAD RESULTS ARE ARCHIVAL. NOT AFFILIATED WITH EITHER UNIVERSITY.</footer>
</section>
<script>
   type TeamId = 'ohio-state' | 'michigan';
   type SeasonProfile = { observed: { conference: string | null; division: string | null; coach: string | null; finalApRank: number | null; cfbdPostseasonRank: number | null; pointsPerGame: number | null; pointsAllowedPerGame: number | null }; derived: { overallRank: number | null; offenseRank: number | null; defenseRank: number | null; scheduleStrengthRank: number | null; ratedTeams: number | null }; confidence: { score: number | null; reasons: string[] } };
   type ProfileEntry = { teamId: TeamId; season: number; profile: SeasonProfile | null };
   type MatchupResponse = { matchup: { ohioState: { expectedScore: number; winProbability: number; scoreAdvantage: number }; michigan: { expectedScore: number; winProbability: number; scoreAdvantage: number }; expectedMargin: number } };
   const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lab]')!; const select = <T extends HTMLElement>(selector: string) => root.querySelector<T>(selector)!;
   const profiles = JSON.parse(root.dataset.seasonProfiles ?? '[]') as ProfileEntry[];
   let matchup: MatchupResponse['matchup']; let lastResult: any; let count = 1;
   const state = () => ({ osuYear: Number(select<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-osu]').value), michYear: Number(select<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mich]').value), seed: select<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]').value });
   const track = (event: string, properties: Record<string, string | number>) => (window as Window & { gtag?: (...args: unknown[]) => void }).gtag?.('event', event, properties);
  async function getMatchup() { const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); const response = await fetch(`/api/matchup?osuYear=${osuYear}&michYear=${michYear}`); const payload = await response.json(); if (!response.ok) throw new Error(payload.error); matchup = payload.matchup; select('[data-osu-year]').textContent = String(osuYear); select('[data-mich-year]').textContent = String(michYear); select('[data-osu-facts]').textContent = `DERIVED OVERALL ${matchup.ohioState.scoreAdvantage.toFixed(1)} · expected ${matchup.ohioState.expectedScore.toFixed(1)} points`; select('[data-mich-facts]').textContent = `DERIVED OVERALL ${matchup.michigan.scoreAdvantage.toFixed(1)} · expected ${matchup.michigan.expectedScore.toFixed(1)} points`; select('[data-context]').textContent = `${osuYear} OHIO STATE × ${michYear} MICHIGAN · ERA NEUTRAL`; renderTape(); renderPregame(); }
  function show(screen: string) { root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-view]').forEach((view) => view.hidden = view.dataset.view !== screen); root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.lab-nav button').forEach((button) => button.setAttribute('aria-current', button.dataset.screen === screen ? 'step' : 'false')); }
  const percentage = (value: number) => `${Math.round(value * 100)}%`;
   function rankLabel(rank: number | null, ratedTeams: number | null) { return rank === null ? 'UNRANKED' : `NO. ${rank}${ratedTeams === null ? '' : ` OF ${ratedTeams}`}`; }
   function profileCard(teamId: TeamId, season: number, teamName: string, color: string) { const profile = profiles.find((entry) => entry.teamId === teamId && entry.season === season)?.profile; if (!profile) return `<article class="season-profile ${color}" data-testid="season-profile-${teamId}"><header><b>${teamName} · ${season}</b><em>PROFILE UNAVAILABLE</em></header><p>This public snapshot has no observed or derived profile for this season.</p></article>`; const { observed, derived, confidence } = profile; const conference = [observed.conference, observed.division].filter(Boolean).join(' · ') || 'Conference not reported'; return `<article class="season-profile ${color}" data-testid="season-profile-${teamId}"><header><b>${teamName} · ${season}</b><em>SEASON PROFILE</em></header><p class="profile-record">${conference} · ${observed.coach ?? 'Coach not reported'}</p><div class="profile-facts"><span><small>OBSERVED SCORING</small><strong>${observed.pointsPerGame === null ? 'NOT REPORTED' : `${observed.pointsPerGame.toFixed(1)} PPG`}</strong><i>${observed.pointsAllowedPerGame === null ? 'Points allowed not reported' : `${observed.pointsAllowedPerGame.toFixed(1)} allowed per game`}</i></span><span><small>OBSERVED FINAL AP</small><strong>${observed.finalApRank === null ? 'UNRANKED' : `NO. ${observed.finalApRank}`}</strong><i>${observed.cfbdPostseasonRank === null ? 'CFBD postseason rank unavailable' : `CFBD postseason: No. ${observed.cfbdPostseasonRank}`}</i></span></div><div class="profile-ranks"><small>DERIVED SRS RANKINGS</small><span>OVERALL <b>${rankLabel(derived.overallRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span><span>OFFENSE <b>${rankLabel(derived.offenseRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span><span>DEFENSE <b>${rankLabel(derived.defenseRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span><span>SCHEDULE <b>${rankLabel(derived.scheduleStrengthRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span></div><p class="profile-confidence"><b>SNAPSHOT CONFIDENCE ${confidence.score === null ? 'NOT SCORED' : `${confidence.score}%`}</b>${confidence.reasons.length ? ` · ${confidence.reasons[0]}` : ''}</p></article>`; }
   function renderProfiles() { const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); select('[data-profiles]').innerHTML = `<div class="section-title"><h2>SEASON PROFILES</h2><span>OBSERVED FACTS · DERIVED RANKINGS</span></div><div class="profile-grid">${profileCard('ohio-state', osuYear, 'OHIO STATE', 'osu')}${profileCard('michigan', michYear, 'MICHIGAN', 'mich')}</div>`; }
   function renderTape() { const rows = [['Expected score', matchup.ohioState.expectedScore, matchup.michigan.expectedScore, 'DERIVED'], ['Win probability', matchup.ohioState.winProbability * 100, matchup.michigan.winProbability * 100, 'DERIVED'], ['Score advantage', matchup.ohioState.scoreAdvantage, matchup.michigan.scoreAdvantage, 'DERIVED']]; select('[data-tape]').innerHTML = `<div class="tape-head"><b class="osu">OHIO STATE</b><b>METRIC · EVIDENCE</b><b class="mich">MICHIGAN</b></div>${rows.map(([name, osu, mich, evidence]) => `<div><strong>${Number(osu).toFixed(1)}</strong><span><u title="Server-derived from public SRS snapshot">${name}</u><em>${evidence}</em></span><strong>${Number(mich).toFixed(1)}</strong></div>`).join('')}`; renderProfiles(); }
  function renderPregame() { select('[data-osu-prob]').textContent = percentage(matchup.ohioState.winProbability); select('[data-mich-prob]').textContent = percentage(matchup.michigan.winProbability); (select<HTMLElement>('[data-osu-bar]')).style.width = percentage(matchup.ohioState.winProbability); (select<HTMLElement>('[data-mich-bar]')).style.width = percentage(matchup.michigan.winProbability); select('[data-score]').innerHTML = `<span class="mich">${Math.round(matchup.michigan.expectedScore)} MICH</span> – <span class="osu">${Math.round(matchup.ohioState.expectedScore)} OSU</span>`; select('[data-osu-driver]').textContent = `${matchup.ohioState.scoreAdvantage.toFixed(1)} translated points above the neutral baseline.`; select('[data-mich-driver]').textContent = `${matchup.michigan.scoreAdvantage.toFixed(1)} translated points above the neutral baseline.`; }
   async function simulate(runCount: number) { count = runCount; const response = await fetch('/api/simulate', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ ...state(), count }) }); const payload = await response.json(); if (!response.ok) throw new Error(payload.error); lastResult = payload.result; const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); track('rivalry_lab_simulation_run', { osu_season: osuYear, michigan_season: michYear, simulation_count: runCount }); if (count === 1) { renderGame(lastResult); show('game'); } else { renderPostgame(lastResult); show('postgame'); } }
  function renderGame(game: any) { select('[data-game-score]').innerHTML = `<div><b class="mich">MICHIGAN</b><strong>${game.michigan.points}</strong></div><span>FINAL<br><small>SIMULATED</small></span><div><b class="osu">OHIO STATE</b><strong>${game.ohioState.points}</strong></div>`; select('[data-timeline]').innerHTML = game.drives.map((drive: any, index: number) => `<i title="Q${drive.quarter} · ${drive.outcome}" class="${drive.teamId === 'michigan' ? 'mich-bg' : 'osu-bg'}" style="animation-delay:${index * 40}ms">${drive.outcome}</i>`).join(''); select('[data-turning]').innerHTML = `<b>KEY TURNING POINT · SIMULATED</b><h3>Q${game.turningPoints.at(-1)?.quarter ?? 4} scoring drive shifts the seeded game state.</h3><p>Seed ${game.seed}. This is synthetic output, not a historical result.</p>`; select('[data-game-stats]').innerHTML = `<b>SIMULATED TEAM STATS</b><p><span>Ohio State</span> ${game.ohioState.possessions} possessions · ${game.ohioState.turnovers} turnovers</p><p><span>Michigan</span> ${game.michigan.possessions} possessions · ${game.michigan.turnovers} turnovers</p>`; }
  function renderPostgame(series: any) { const total = series.games.length; const mich = (series.michigan.wins / total * 100).toFixed(1); const osu = (series.ohioState.wins / total * 100).toFixed(1); select('[data-series-context]').textContent = `${total.toLocaleString()}-SIMULATION SERIES · SEED ${series.seed} · DRIVE-V1`; select('[data-post-panel]').innerHTML = `<div class="series"><div><strong class="mich">${series.michigan.wins.toLocaleString()}</strong><b>MICHIGAN WINS · ${mich}%</b></div><div><strong class="osu">${series.ohioState.wins.toLocaleString()}</strong><b>OHIO STATE WINS · ${osu}%</b></div></div><div class="prob-bar"><i style="width:${mich}%" class="mich-bg"></i><i style="width:${osu}%" class="osu-bg"></i></div><p>SIMULATED: ${series.oneScoreGames} one-score games · ${series.overtimeGames} overtime games · ${series.blowoutGames} games decided by 17+.</p>`; }
   root.addEventListener('click', async (event) => { const target = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('button'); if (!target) return; try { if (target.dataset.screen) show(target.dataset.screen); if (target.matches('[data-build]')) { await getMatchup(); const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); track('rivalry_lab_matchup_built', { osu_season: osuYear, michigan_season: michYear, era_mode: 'neutral' }); show('tape'); } if (target.matches('[data-pregame]')) { await getMatchup(); show('pregame'); } if (target.dataset.run) await simulate(Number(target.dataset.run)); if (target.matches('[data-rerun]')) { select<HTMLInputElement>('[data-seed]').value = String(Math.floor(10_000_000 + Math.random() * 89_999_999)); await simulate(1); } if (target.matches('[data-postgame]')) { await simulate(10000); } } catch (error) { alert(error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unable to run Rivalry Lab'); } });
   select('[data-osu]').addEventListener('change', () => void getMatchup()); select('[data-mich]').addEventListener('change', () => void getMatchup()); select<HTMLDetailsElement>('[data-chalk]').addEventListener('toggle', async (event) => { if (!(event.currentTarget as HTMLDetailsElement).open || !matchup) return; const response = await fetch('/api/chalk-talk', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ matchup, simulation: count === 1 ? lastResult : undefined }) }); const payload = await response.json(); const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); track('rivalry_lab_chalk_talk_opened', { osu_season: osuYear, michigan_season: michYear, simulation_count: count }); select('[data-chalk-panel]').innerHTML = payload.panel.map((item: any) => `<article><b>${item.role}</b><p><em>${item.evidenceType}:</em> ${item.text}</p></article>`).join(''); });
  void getMatchup();
</script>

<style is:global>
   .selector-box select { font-size:24px; }
   .season-profiles { margin-top: 36px; }.profile-grid { display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px;margin-top:14px; }.season-profile { border:3px solid #111;padding:20px; }.season-profile.osu { border-top-color:#bb0000; }.season-profile.mich { border-top-color:#00274c; }.season-profile header,.profile-facts,.profile-ranks span { display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px; }.season-profile header b { font:20px 'Archivo Black'; }.season-profile em,.profile-facts small,.profile-ranks small { color:#6b717c;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em; }.profile-record { margin:12px 0 16px; }.profile-facts { border-top:1px solid #d9dce1;border-bottom:1px solid #d9dce1;padding:12px 0; }.profile-facts span { display:grid;gap:3px; }.profile-facts strong { font:18px 'Archivo Black'; }.profile-facts i { color:#6b717c;font-size:12px;font-style:normal; }.profile-ranks { display:grid;gap:8px;padding-top:14px; }.profile-ranks span { font-size:12px;font-weight:700; }.profile-ranks b { font-family:'Archivo Black'; }.profile-confidence { border-top:1px solid #d9dce1;margin:14px 0 0;padding-top:12px;color:#6b717c;font-size:12px; }
   @media (max-width:640px) { .selector-box select { font-size:22px; } }
   @media (max-width:640px) { .profile-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; }.profile-facts { gap:18px; }.season-profile { padding:16px; } }
</style>
